1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:02,997
What if your reflection lived one day ahead?

2
00:00:03,037 --> 00:00:04,328
You brush your teeth,

3
00:00:04,368 --> 00:00:07,432
glance up, and your reflection is already wearing

4
00:00:07,472 --> 00:00:09,206
a party hat and eating cake.

5
00:00:09,246 --> 00:00:10,663
That is tomorrow's you.

6
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:13,507
Soon it gets useful.

7
00:00:13,547 --> 00:00:15,743
Your reflection holds up a sign:

8
00:00:15,783 --> 00:00:17,281
bus nine will be late.

9
00:00:17,321 --> 00:00:19,586
You leave later, finish your tea,

10
00:00:19,626 --> 00:00:21,892
and still arrive exactly on time.

11
00:00:21,932 --> 00:00:23,569
Smugness level: maximum.

12
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:25,306
Then it gets greedy.

13
00:00:25,346 --> 00:00:27,832
Your reflection waves a lottery ticket.

14
00:00:27,872 --> 00:00:29,192
You copy the numbers,

15
00:00:29,232 --> 00:00:31,913
buy the ticket, and feel like the smartest

16
00:00:31,953 --> 00:00:33,079
person in history.

17
00:00:33,119 --> 00:00:34,763
Hypothetically, of course.

18
00:00:35,250 --> 00:00:37,307
But then you change your mind.

19
00:00:37,347 --> 00:00:40,313
The reflection freezes, scratches its head,

20
00:00:40,353 --> 00:00:41,711
and holds up a sign:

21
00:00:41,751 --> 00:00:43,318
that is not what I did.

22
00:00:43,358 --> 00:00:46,254
Apparently, tomorrow is only a suggestion.

23
00:00:46,750 --> 00:00:49,388
You start to notice how tired it looks.

24
00:00:49,428 --> 00:00:51,653
It lives every day before you do,

25
00:00:51,693 --> 00:00:53,370
and never gets surprised.

26
00:00:53,410 --> 00:00:55,155
It holds up one last sign:

27
00:00:55,195 --> 00:00:56,459
I miss not knowing.

28
00:00:58,250 --> 00:01:01,286
One morning the sign says something different:

29
00:01:01,326 --> 00:01:02,556
call Grandpa today.

30
00:01:02,596 --> 00:01:03,759
You don't ask why.

31
00:01:03,799 --> 00:01:06,634
You pick up the phone and talk for an hour.

32
00:01:06,674 --> 00:01:09,175
Some forecasts are better as warnings.

33
00:01:10,150 --> 00:01:11,420
Then comes the twist.

34
00:01:11,460 --> 00:01:14,041
The reflection steps out of the mirror and

35
00:01:14,081 --> 00:01:15,352
sits down beside you.

36
00:01:15,392 --> 00:01:16,974
It was never ahead of you.

37
00:01:17,014 --> 00:01:20,094
It was just patiently waiting for you to catch up.

38
00:01:22,850 --> 00:01:25,460
Maybe that's the real thought experiment.

39
00:01:25,500 --> 00:01:28,111
The future isn't a prophecy in the glass.

40
00:01:28,151 --> 00:01:29,856
It's someone who loves you,

41
00:01:29,896 --> 00:01:31,214
standing a day ahead,

42
00:01:31,254 --> 00:01:33,541
saying: come on, I saved you a seat.
